{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787603600637217001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"spoiled-bionic-goose","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"c527edc39bdc003f989361c1765a9fcbb95d31b9d4dc29663d07ec802d721860","event_uuid":"269fee0c-cd1f-40a6-a208-cde5d738eb85","position":{"commit_sha":"5800f4ada85ae3be44cd75d61dce896467cca5d9","position":"1787598378653058001-269fee0c-cd1f-40a6-a208-cde5d738eb85"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ad25efaa45be7bf22816da79cd4012387feeba626916e916222613ff421b8316","event_uuid":"40735fb9-2b76-4d5b-965f-7582063c78e8","position":{"commit_sha":"6dd05c70c40725e422ecde5b074e69d4fa703468","position":"1787598439813802001-40735fb9-2b76-4d5b-965f-7582063c78e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c021c7785e977a3f6a403d2dfb47d034b8034c650dc1d11271e82623ec7bddd4","event_uuid":"23f71c5d-177e-4d36-829a-9774266b24f9","position":{"commit_sha":"e4615e84043fecbfeb42414517a93de570a7e92d","position":"1787600395453738001-23f71c5d-177e-4d36-829a-9774266b24f9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787598378653058001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"40735fb9-2b76-4d5b-965f-7582063c78e8","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"}],"description":"Register the AWS box as a trusted signing environment so plan-review and completion-verifier op-certs\nminted via the on-box MCP server are ENFORCEABLE (ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur, decision 3; ADR\n0049). Without this, MCP-minted certs are not trusted and certified ops through MCP are\nunenforceable. Single concern: the trust-environment provisioning + config — distinct from the MCP\nservice (esok) and the client auth (avians).\n\n## Approach + rationale\nPer ADR 0049, an op-cert is only enforceable when the signing environment is registered and\n`verify.require_environment` is on. Provision the box's opcert signing key (out-of-band, like the\nexisting opcert service key), pin its PUBLIC key in `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` on `main`\n(the authoritative-state file), and confirm `verify.require_environment` is enabled so a cert minted\nby the box verifies and a cert from an unregistered environment does not. This is additive to the\nexisting opcert trust path (which coexists); it does not change how the two existing op-cert kinds\nare issued, only that the box is now a recognized signer for MCP-minted certs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **real signing + verification round-trip** (test-design §3 \"external-service mapping\" done as\n  an in-process crypto round-trip). Oracles:\n  - `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` on `main` contains the box's environment id + its PUBLIC key\n    only (assert no private key material is committed — negative control, §6).\n  - A plan-review/completion cert signed by the box's key VERIFIES under `verify.require_environment`\n    (positive), and an otherwise-identical cert signed by an UNREGISTERED key is REJECTED (contrast,\n    §6) — asserted through the real verify path, not a stub.\n- [ ] The private signing key is provisioned out-of-band (SSM / secret store), never committed (guard as\n  in avians).\n\n## Compat / rollback / migration-safety\nAdditive registration; existing opcert/remote-cert trust path unchanged (regression oracle: an\nexisting opcert-minted cert still verifies). Rollback = remove the box's entry from\n`.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` (MCP-minted certs then stop verifying; existing paths unaffected).\nApproval-gated: touches the authoritative trust config on `main` + provisions a signing key (a human\nperforms the key provisioning).\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR). Blocks: inadequate-hydrated-starling (guidance asserts\ncertified ops are enforceable via MCP, true only once the box is a trusted env).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"],["parent","jira-reb-3527"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-3527","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b173-e50a-4b93-455f","ticket_type":"task","title":"Register the AWS box as a trusted signing environment (enforceable MCP-minted op-certs)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["269fee0c-cd1f-40a6-a208-cde5d738eb85","40735fb9-2b76-4d5b-965f-7582063c78e8","23f71c5d-177e-4d36-829a-9774266b24f9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787603600637217001,"uuid":"ec173f1e-b854-4587-b9ba-7547ab75c691"}